antagonism in macaque cone photoreceptors. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>In press</volume>.</citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Verweij, J., M. Kamermans, and H. Spekrejse. <year>1996</year>. Horizontal cells feed back to cones by shifting the cones calcium-current activation range. <source>Vision Res.</source> <volume>36</volume>:<fpage>3943</fpage>&#x02013;3953.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9068848</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Werblin, F.S., and J.E. Dowling. <year>1969</year>. Organization of the retina of the mudpuppy, Necturus maculosus. II. Intracellular recording. <source>J. Neurophysiol.</source> <volume>32</volume>:<fpage>339</fpage>&#x02013;355.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4306897</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Wilkinson, M.F., and S. Barnes. <year>1996</year>. The dihydropyridine-sensitive calcium channel subtype in cone photoreceptors. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>107</volume>:<fpage>621</fpage>&#x02013;630.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8740375</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>